# Line endings.
#
# Added Sep 12 2026. Before this, the repo had no line-ending policy at all,
# and the result was 13 files sitting in CRLF among ~360 in LF -- app/layout.tsx,
# app/components/Footer.tsx, app/account/page.tsx, lib/money-score.ts and
# friends -- with app/api/money-score/submit/route.ts carrying DOUBLED \r\r\n
# endings, which no editor produces on purpose.
#
# The cost was not cosmetic. Any tool that rewrites a file (a codemod, a
# find-and-replace script, an editor with a different default) flips that
# file's endings wholesale, so a genuine 27-line change lands as a 481-line
# diff. Real edits become unreviewable, `git blame` loses the history of every
# line in the file, and two people editing the same file conflict on all of it
# rather than on the part they both touched. That happened here.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git the authority: it normalizes to LF on commit
# and checks out LF everywhere, Windows included. Modern Windows tooling --
# VS Code, PowerShell, Node, Next.js -- all handle LF fine, so there is no
# reason to keep CRLF in the working tree.
#
# One-time step to apply this to the files already committed:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalize line endings to LF"
#
# Do that as its OWN commit, separate from any real change, or the real change
# will be buried in exactly the noise this file exists to end.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the genuine exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse a .bat
# with LF endings, and android/gradlew.bat is one of these.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even when checked out on Windows -- android/gradlew
# is run by CI and by macOS/Linux builds.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Generated. Marking the lockfile as such keeps a dependency bump from
# rendering as thousands of reviewable lines in a pull request.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
